            `// UNSAFE:` (why it cannot be safe) and `// SAFETY:` (why it is sound). Right above: \
            the comment lines directly over the statement or item the site starts (no blank line \
            between), comments inside that statement before the site, or one ending its line. The \
            first five are reported one by one, then one warning counts the rest; an error with \
            --deny-warnings. std's sites are not the program's: `volec query unsafe std` lists \
            them.",
        fix: b"Try the safe way first (std's APIs, Vec, slices, a borrow); `volec query unsafe \
